een revoked"},"6655":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting-39","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting#535-authentication-failed","content":"Copy the API key again; whitespace or trailing characters can cause failures"},"6656":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting-40","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting#553-authentication-required","content":"You are trying to send without authenticating first. Ensure your SMTP client is configured to use authentication with LOGIN or PLAIN mechanism."},"6657":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting-41","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting#api-key-format-invalid","content":"API keys follow the format `nr_live_xxxxxxxxxxxx`. If your key does not start with `nr_live_`, it may be a test key or an old key format. Generate a new key from **Dashboard → API Keys**."},"6658":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting-42","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting#emails-landing-in-spam","content":"This is almost always caused by missing or incorrect DNS authentication records."},"6659":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting-43","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting#emails-landing-in-spam","content":"**Set up SPF** — Add a TXT record to your domain:"},"6660":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting-44","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/troubleshooting#emails-landing-in-spam","content":"**Verify DKIM** — DKIM is auto-configured when you verify your domain in the dashboard. Confirm the DKIM record is published:"},"6661":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/trou