sses are authorized to send email for your domain."},"6774":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-49","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"Add a TXT record at the root of your domain:"},"6775":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-50","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"Field"},"6776":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-51","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"Value"},"6777":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-52","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"**Type**"},"6778":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-53","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"TXT"},"6779":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-54","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"**Host/Name**"},"6780":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-55","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"`@` (or leave blank, depending on your DNS provider)"},"6781":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-56","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"**Value**"},"6782":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-57","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"`v=spf1 include:_spf.north-pipe.ca -all`"},"6783":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-58","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"**TTL**"},"6784":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-59","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"3600 (or default)"},"6785":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-60","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#how-it-works","content":"The `include:_spf.north-pipe.ca` directive tells receiving servers to look up NorthRelay's SPF record, which lists NorthRelay's sending IPs (IPv4 and IPv6), so you never need to update SPF when our infrastructure changes. The `-all` suffix means \"reject email from any other source\" — this is the strictest and most secure setting."},"6786":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-61","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#if-you-already-have-an-spf-record","content":"A domain can only have **one** SPF TXT record. If you already send email through another provider, merge the records:"},"6787":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-62","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#if-you-already-have-an-spf-record","content":"Do not create a second TXT record starting with `v=spf1` — this will cause SPF to fail entirely."},"6788":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-63","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#common-mistakes","content":"Using `~all` (softfail) instead of `-all` (hardfail) — softfail is weaker and may not protect you"},"6789":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-64","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#common-mistakes","content":"Adding more than 10 DNS lookups in your SPF chain (SPF has a 10-lookup limit)"},"6790":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-65","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#common-mistakes","content":"Creating multiple SPF records on the same domain"},"6791":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-66","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dkim-record","content":"DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail) adds a cryptographic signature to each outgoing email, allowing the recipient to verify the message was not altered in transit."},"6792":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-67","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"DKIM is **automatically configured** when you verify your domain in the NorthRelay dashboard. After verification, NorthRelay publishes the DKIM public key and signs all outgoing email from your domain."},"6793":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-68","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"To verify your domain:"},"6794":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-69","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"Go to **Dashboard → Domains**"},"6795":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-70","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"Click **Add Domain** and enter your domain name"},"6796":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-71","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"Add the verification TXT record shown in the dashboard to your DNS"},"6797":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-72","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"Click **Verify**"},"6798":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-73","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"Once verified, DKIM signing is enabled automatically"},"6799":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-74","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#verifying-dkim","content":"After domain verification, confirm the DKIM record is published:"},"6800":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-75","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#verifying-dkim","content":"You should see a response containing a `v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=...` value. If the record is missing, wait up to 48 hours for DNS propagation, then check again."},"6801":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-76","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#subdomains","content":"DKIM signing supports subdomains automatically. If you send from `notifications@sub.yourdomain.com`, the parent domain's DKIM key will sign the email (using the `SubDomains=yes` configuration on NorthRelay's signing infrastructure)."},"6802":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-77","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dmarc-record","content":"DMARC (Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance) tells receiving servers how to handle emails that fail SPF or DKIM checks, and where to send aggregate reports."},"6803":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-78","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"Add a TXT record at `_dmarc.yourdomain.com`:"},"6804":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-79","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"Field"},"6805":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-80","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"Value"},"6806":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-81","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"**Type**"},"6807":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-82","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"TXT"},"6808":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-83","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"**Host/Name**"},"6809":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-84","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setu